00:29:59.410 --> 00:29:59.960
Yeah?

00:30:00.550 --> 00:30:02.410
Corbett's a --
he's a death echo.

00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:04.970
He's reliving his own murder.

00:30:05.790 --> 00:30:07.120
Over and over forever.

00:30:12.340 --> 00:30:13.930
What's this Daggett
guy's problem anyway?

00:30:15.070 --> 00:30:15.740
Loneliness.

00:30:16.380 --> 00:30:17.410
He's never heard of a realdoll?

00:30:17.690 --> 00:30:19.990
No, no, no, Daggett
was the norman bates,

00:30:20.350 --> 00:30:21.750
Stuff-your-mother
kind of lonely.

00:30:21.970 --> 00:30:25.350
That's why he lifted these
bodies from the morgue,

00:30:25.580 --> 00:30:26.519
Threw himself a birthday party,

00:30:26.890 --> 00:30:28.380
Except they were the
only ones who would come.

00:30:29.050 --> 00:30:31.990
Anyway, so, at midnight, he
sealed them   in the bomb shelter

00:30:32.150 --> 00:30:34.009
And went upstairs and
o.d.'d on horse tranqs.

00:30:35.040 --> 00:30:35.509
How do you know this?

00:30:36.290 --> 00:30:37.090
Cause he told me.

00:30:38.140 --> 00:30:38.920
Oh. yeah.

00:30:39.660 --> 00:30:41.160
Okay, so now that he's dead, what?

00:30:41.340 --> 00:30:42.779
Same song, different verse,

00:30:42.980 --> 00:30:44.090
Trying to get people
to come to his party?

00:30:44.310 --> 00:30:45.690
Pretty much, yeah. stay forever.

00:30:47.170 --> 00:30:48.220
Are those real bullets?

00:30:49.170 --> 00:30:49.650
It's rock salt.

00:31:06.110 --> 00:31:06.690
Oh, no.

00:31:07.140 --> 00:31:08.080
Oh, god.

00:31:12.730 --> 00:31:13.400
Wait, guys.

00:31:15.259 --> 00:31:17.180
Guys, it's --
it's Corbett.

00:31:18.730 --> 00:31:20.450
He's -- he's
-- he's trapped.

00:31:20.540 --> 00:31:21.380
He's in a lot of pain, you know?

00:31:21.460 --> 00:31:22.810
We got to
try and --

00:31:22.900 --> 00:31:25.640
We got to try and pull
him out of his loop.

00:31:28.860 --> 00:31:29.450
We have to.

00:31:32.720 --> 00:31:34.279
Corbett.

00:31:36.850 --> 00:31:37.680
Corbett,
it's --

00:31:39.140 --> 00:31:39.690
Oh, god.

00:31:40.120 --> 00:31:40.990
Don't cross the line of salt.

00:31:43.570 --> 00:31:45.190
Corbett, listen to me.

00:31:46.040 --> 00:31:46.980
Okay, I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:31:47.970 --> 00:31:48.480
Listen.

00:31:50.259 --> 00:31:52.410
Listen. oh, god. Corbett.

00:31:53.779 --> 00:31:55.000
Oh. oh, god. whoa.

00:31:55.890 --> 00:31:57.730
Oh, I can't, okay?

00:31:59.570 --> 00:32:00.610
He's not hearing me, okay?

00:32:00.980 --> 00:32:02.090
He won't stop dying.

00:32:07.980 --> 00:32:09.860
Seriously -- you're
still shooting?

00:32:10.390 --> 00:32:11.840
It makes him feel
better. don't ask.

00:32:18.630 --> 00:32:19.820
Ah, hell, guys.

00:32:19.930 --> 00:32:21.880
Get in your ghost-role
thing. something's coming.

00:32:22.900 --> 00:32:23.630
Oh,
my --

00:32:35.320 --> 00:32:36.790
I know how we can
get through to him.

00:32:37.370 --> 00:32:37.870
How?

00:32:38.550 --> 00:32:39.029
Ed...

00:32:41.779 --> 00:32:42.820
He had feelings for you.

00:32:46.190 --> 00:32:47.470
He wanted you.

00:32:48.720 --> 00:32:49.850
Wa-- wanted
me to what?

00:32:50.009 --> 00:32:50.490
You know.

00:32:54.380 --> 00:32:55.240
And you know what you've got to do.

00:32:57.810 --> 00:32:58.519
You can do it, Ed.

00:33:00.380 --> 00:33:01.769
You've always been the
brave one. yes, you can.

00:33:02.230 --> 00:33:04.190
You make us brave
-- Maggie, right?

00:33:04.380 --> 00:33:05.990
Yeah.

00:33:06.750 --> 00:33:07.300
Ed...

00:33:08.840 --> 00:33:11.100
You got to go be gay for
that poor, dead intern.

00:33:11.630 --> 00:33:13.160
You got to send him into the light.

00:33:32.670 --> 00:33:33.269
Corbett.

00:33:34.340 --> 00:33:35.080
Maggie, no. no.

00:33:35.560 --> 00:33:36.420
It's okay.

00:33:37.930 --> 00:33:38.700
Corbett, look.

00:33:39.340 --> 00:33:41.380
Hey, it's just Ed,
buddy. it's just me.

00:33:42.420 --> 00:33:44.970
Hey, hey, Corbett, listen
to me. listen to me.

00:33:45.330 --> 00:33:46.650
I --
we...

00:33:50.190 --> 00:33:50.769
Okay.

00:33:51.740 --> 00:33:52.410
You meant...

00:33:54.690 --> 00:33:56.130
Corbett, you meant
a lot to the team.

00:34:00.120 --> 00:34:00.730
You meant...

00:34:03.180 --> 00:34:04.210
You meant a lot to me.

00:34:04.890 --> 00:34:06.580
You know, never back down...

00:34:08.509 --> 00:34:10.460
Never say a bad word, okay?

00:34:10.610 --> 00:34:13.820
I remember that, Corbett.
i-i remember that.

00:34:13.969 --> 00:34:15.579
I remember because
I love you, Corbett.

00:34:16.929 --> 00:34:19.150
I really, truly love you.

00:34:23.559 --> 00:34:25.129
Do you remember that? do you?

00:34:27.029 --> 00:34:28.500
Hey. Ed?

00:34:28.869 --> 00:34:29.409
Yeah.

00:34:31.159 --> 00:34:32.250
Yeah, Corbett, it's...

00:34:34.940 --> 00:34:36.019
Corbett, yeah, it's me.

00:34:37.599 --> 00:34:39.039
It's me. look at me.

00:34:42.190 --> 00:34:44.849
You got to help us, man.
you have to help us, Corbett.

00:34:45.179 --> 00:34:46.139
Please. please.

00:34:47.269 --> 00:34:48.420
Please help us right now.

00:34:49.839 --> 00:34:50.579
Take it easy. you all right?

00:34:51.980 --> 00:34:53.429
Uh, guys...

00:34:59.129 --> 00:35:00.739
This is bad
-- very bad.

00:35:07.929 --> 00:35:09.179
Corbett?

00:35:19.949 --> 00:35:20.519
You all right, dude?

00:35:23.230 --> 00:35:23.730
You all right?

00:35:30.579 --> 00:35:31.309
God.

00:35:49.089 --> 00:35:53.049
Leap year, february
29th, the Morton house.

00:35:53.619 --> 00:35:54.500
A tragic
day --

00:35:55.389 --> 00:35:58.339
A day of souls bound in torment,

00:35:58.719 --> 00:36:01.609
Of lives held in cruel balance.

00:36:02.909 --> 00:36:03.899
But the
Ghostfacers --

00:36:04.019 --> 00:36:05.309
They did the best that they could.

00:36:06.750 --> 00:36:09.339
We lost a beloved friend,

00:36:10.629 --> 00:36:13.609
But we gained new allies.

00:36:14.000 --> 00:36:15.059
We know
this much --

00:36:16.009 --> 00:36:18.369
That every day, including today,

00:36:19.109 --> 00:36:20.059
Is a new beginning.

00:36:21.739 --> 00:36:23.940
We learned more than we can say

00:36:24.170 --> 00:36:25.989
In the brutal feat
of the morton house.

00:36:27.509 --> 00:36:30.869
The Ghostfacers were
forced to face something

00:36:31.599 --> 00:36:34.329
Far more scary than ghosts.

00:36:35.839 --> 00:36:37.289
They were forced
to face themselves.

00:36:39.409 --> 00:36:40.829
War changes man.

00:36:42.139 --> 00:36:43.259
And Maggie.

00:36:44.929 --> 00:36:47.230
War changes man...

00:36:48.879 --> 00:36:49.639
And one woman.

00:36:52.829 --> 00:36:53.989
You know, Corbett, we just...

00:36:55.909 --> 00:36:57.509
Oh, gosh, we just like to think

00:36:57.629 --> 00:36:59.089
That you're out there
watching over us.

00:37:00.469 --> 00:37:00.889
As far as we're concerned,

00:37:01.869 --> 00:37:03.089
You're not an intern anymore.

00:37:04.569 --> 00:37:07.440
You have more than earned
full Ghostfacer status.

00:37:09.079 --> 00:37:10.420
Plus, it'd be cool to
have a ghost on the team.

00:37:10.579 --> 00:37:11.019
Yeah.

00:37:11.889 --> 00:37:12.679
You know, and here we were,

00:37:12.799 --> 00:37:15.449
Thinking that, you know,
we were teaching you,

00:37:15.489 --> 00:37:17.389
And all this time,

00:37:17.539 --> 00:37:18.670
You were teaching us...

00:37:20.129 --> 00:37:21.579
About heart,

00:37:22.250 --> 00:37:25.129
About dedication, and...

00:37:27.259 --> 00:37:31.940
About how gay love can pierce
through the veil of death

00:37:32.989 --> 00:37:33.949
And save the day.

00:37:36.619 --> 00:37:38.299
Thank you, alan j. Corbett.

00:37:39.599 --> 00:37:42.690
Go well into that
starry night, young turk.

00:37:45.219 --> 00:37:45.730
Go well.

00:37:54.399 --> 00:37:55.480
Come on, Spruce.

00:37:55.690 --> 00:37:57.449
I got to get all
this stuff packed up.

00:37:57.809 --> 00:37:59.109
So? pack and talk.

00:37:59.829 --> 00:38:00.670
I don't know what to say.

00:38:01.109 --> 00:38:01.909
Say what comes to mind.

00:38:03.219 --> 00:38:05.099
This is one of our
confessional moments, Corbett,

00:38:05.239 --> 00:38:06.039
So confess.

00:38:06.960 --> 00:38:08.769
What do you think was
gonna happen tonight?

00:38:08.869 --> 00:38:11.159
What do you think's gonna
happen tonight on this trip?

00:38:13.239 --> 00:38:15.589
I think tonight
-- I really do --

00:38:16.469 --> 00:38:17.769
I think all our dreams
are gonna come true.

00:38:20.730 --> 00:38:21.480
Does that sound stupid?

00:38:22.639 --> 00:38:23.429
Kind of does, yeah.

00:38:46.769 --> 00:38:47.859
So, guys, what do you think?

00:38:50.069 --> 00:38:50.629
You all right?

00:38:51.980 --> 00:38:53.309
You know, I kind of
think it was half awesome.

00:38:54.099 --> 00:38:56.429
Half awesome -- that's
full-on good, right?

00:38:57.730 --> 00:38:58.149
Yeah.

00:38:58.349 --> 00:39:00.089
I mean, it's bizarre
how y'all are able to --

00:39:00.500 --> 00:39:03.159
To honor Corbett's memory while
grossly exploiting the manner of his

00:39:03.299 --> 00:39:04.119
death.

00:39:04.389 --> 00:39:04.849
Well done.

00:39:05.289 --> 00:39:07.289
Yeah, that's a real tight
rope you guys are walking.

00:39:07.519 --> 00:39:09.049
Yeah. all right, guys.

00:39:11.639 --> 00:39:14.230
No, that's reality, man. yeah.

00:39:14.469 --> 00:39:15.969
Corbett gave his life
searching for the truth,

00:39:16.269 --> 00:39:19.409
And it is our job over here
to share it with the world.

00:39:20.389 --> 00:39:22.619
Right. well, um,
our experience --

00:39:22.989 --> 00:39:24.629
You know what you get when
you show the world the truth?

00:39:24.949 --> 00:39:27.139
A straightjacket or
a punch in the face --

00:39:27.250 --> 00:39:28.250
Sometimes both. right.

00:39:28.469 --> 00:39:30.980
Oh, come on, guys,
don't be 'facer haters

00:39:31.139 --> 00:39:33.369
Because we happen to have gotten
the footage of the century.

00:39:33.929 --> 00:39:34.420
Oh, yeah.

00:39:38.039 --> 00:39:39.029
You got us there. yeah.

00:39:39.219 --> 00:39:41.109
Yeah, well, we'll
see you guys around.

00:39:52.409 --> 00:39:53.039
Dicks.

00:39:54.319 --> 00:39:55.049
Oh, yeah.

00:39:55.149 --> 00:39:55.769
Yeah. yep.

00:39:56.309 --> 00:39:57.579
Start laying off some dvds.

00:39:57.670 --> 00:39:59.519
Sounds like a good idea, Spruce.

00:40:00.509 --> 00:40:03.049
You know, guys, I think we're gonna
need a bigger office here, you know,

00:40:03.099 --> 00:40:04.009
Cause we're gonna go national,

00:40:04.259 --> 00:40:06.440
And then it's gonna go
international, and then --

00:40:06.829 --> 00:40:08.480
Hey, menudo left
their dance bag behind.

00:40:10.699 --> 00:40:11.889
What's inside, huh?

00:40:16.179 --> 00:40:17.079
What the hell is this?

00:40:17.769 --> 00:40:21.319
Uh, I seem to be having some
technical difficulty over here.

00:40:23.019 --> 00:40:24.129
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:40:24.299 --> 00:40:25.389
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:40:25.710 --> 00:40:26.730
Wait! wait! wait! wait! wait!

00:40:26.920 --> 00:40:28.289
"no operating system
found"? wait a minute.

00:40:30.980 --> 00:40:31.460
We clean?

00:40:31.879 --> 00:40:32.489

No-o-o-o-o-o-o!

00:40:39.329 --> 00:40:41.149
Electromagnet wiped out every
tape and hard drive they have.

00:40:41.589 --> 00:40:43.099
World just isn't ready
for the Ghostfacers.

00:40:43.779 --> 00:40:45.859
That's too bad. I
kind of liked the show.

